   "subject": "Re: poppr::info_table with recoded data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It would be good If I actually posted the code to set this up...<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Pinf&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;poppr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>plt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> info_table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Pinf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ploidy&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> plot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Retain tetraploid status</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinf </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> recode_polyploids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Pinf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><br>On Wednesday, July 8, 2015 at 10:42:16 AM UTC-7, Zhian Kamvar wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I realized I had replied to Federico only and not the group in general. Recoded data should work in poppr version 2.0. The previous version 1.1 simply would attempt to count the zero alleles present in the data to avoid rounding errors. Since the new version of adegenet represents data as counts of alleles instead of frequencies, the calculation has become simpler as reporting the number of observed alleles. In version 2.0, the following code will work:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">pltr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> info_table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ploidy&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> plot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Assign ploidy of samples based on highest observed</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> recode_polyploids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Pinf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> newploidy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is a genclone object</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># -------------------------</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   Genotype information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   72 multilocus genotypes </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   86 triploid (55) and diploid (31) individuals</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   11 codominant loci</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Population information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 strata - Continent Country</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 populations defined - South America North America</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pltrn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> info_table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinfn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ploidy&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> plot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Both can go back</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>recode_polyploids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addzero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is a genclone object</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># -------------------------</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   Genotype information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   72 original multilocus genotypes </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   86 tetraploid individuals</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   11 codominant loci</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Population information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 strata - Continent Country</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 populations defined - South America North America</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>recode_polyploids</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">iPinfn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addzero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This is a genclone object</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># -------------------------</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   Genotype information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   72 original multilocus genotypes </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   86 triploid individuals</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   11 codominant loci</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Population information:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 strata - Continent Country</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   2 populations defined - South America North America</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>Hope that helps!</div><div>Zhian</div><div><br><br>On Friday, June 12, 2015 at 10:09:21 AM UTC-7, Federico Urban wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Since the info_table function is pretty valid for displaying ploidy I&#39;ve tried to use it with recoded data with the following commands<div><br></div><div>data(Pinf)</div><div><br></div><div>iPinf &lt;- recode_polyploids(Pinf)</div><div><br></div><div>info_table(iPinf, type = &quot;ploidy&quot;, plot = TRUE, low = &quot;black&quot;, high = &quot;orange&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>this will produce the following error:</div><div><br></div><div>Error: test_zeroes(x) is not TRUE<br></div><div><br></div><div>How to fix this?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The fact that I&#39;m using ploidy analysis with recoded data is because the original data will present zeros that are not real allele information but missing information.</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks for who can help me.</div><div><br></div><div>Federico</div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
